Non-sealable: a GitHub Actions OIDC token can only be minted inside an Actions runner, where GitHub injects the ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_* variables, and Pomerium must reach token.actions.githubusercontent.com to fetch the issuer's JWKS, so neither side of the flow can run in the sealed fixture harness. Validated manually 2026-08-12 against a live Core deployment: the guide's workflow returned HTTP 200 and Pomerium logged allow=true with allow-why-true=["claim-ok"] for the github-actions/<sub> identity.
